ist and conservationist Dave Goulson has written an accessible, fascinating, and important book that examines the evidence of an alarming drop in insect numbers around the world. \"If we lose the insects, then everything is going to collapse,\" he warned in a recent interview in the New York Times—beginning with humans' food supply. The main cause of this decrease in insect populations is the indiscriminate use of chemical pesticides. Hence, Silent Earth's nod to Rachel Carson's classic Silent Spring which, when published in 1962, led to the global banning of DDT. This was a huge victory for science and ecological health at the time.","thumbnailUrl":"/book-covers/book-silent-earth-averting-the-insect-apocalypse-dave-goulson.jpg","displaySummary":"The main cause of this decrease in insect populations is the indiscriminate use of chemical pesticides. Hence, Silent Earth's nod to Rachel Carson's classic Silent Spring which, when published in 1962, led to the global banning of DDT. This was a huge victory for science and ecological health at the time.","primarySubject":"Nature & Environment","primaryTopic":"Natural History & Animals","subjectEvidence":{"primarySubject":"Nature & Environment","confidence":"medium","method":"evidence_score","candidates":[{"subject":"Nature & Environment","score":6,"evidenceCount":1}],"evidence":[{"source":"google_books","scheme":"google_books_category","rawLabel":"Nature","mappedSubject":"Nature & Environment","score":6,"confidence":"high","sourceId":"source-google-books-silent-earth-averting-the-insect-apocalypse-dave-goulson","id":"subject-evidence-book-silent-earth-averting-the-insect-apocalypse-dave-goulson-1"},{"source":"keyword_classifier","rawLabel":"Medicine & Public Health","mappedSubject":"Medicine & Public Health","score":2,"confidence":"low","note":"world history keyword; science keyword; medicine/public health keyword; nature/environment keyword","id":"subject-evidence-book-silent-earth-averting-the-insect-apocalypse-dave-gou